From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 20:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] background: Style and Background as pages of their own

Plinius: Appearance was one long page - the animated effect, the style
previews, the accent colors and every background tile one below the
other. It now starts with two rows that say what is set and open pages
of their own (back arrow and back swipe lead back):

- Style: light or dark and the accent color, GNOME's groups as they
  were (subtitle "Dark · Blue", a dot in the accent color in front).
- Background: five sections that open each on its own (AdwExpanderRow,
  the chooser is now an AdwPreferencesGroup): Animated (the effect of
  plinius-ambient over whatever the background is, with the amount;
  before a group on the main page), Video (plinius-ambient 0.5, key
  video-enabled), 360° Photos, Own Pictures and GNOME's Default
  Pictures. Opening the page opens the section of the current
  background, and Animated while an effect is on. Video, 360° Photos
  and Own Pictures each end with their own "Add ..." row. The row on
  the main page shows the background small with its kind and effect.

The tiles of a section are made when it is opened the first time, so
opening Appearance creates none of them (the 360° photos and videos
also read their folders only then).

Removing an own picture asks first (no undo toast any more); removing
the picture shown goes back to GNOME's default one. The app overview
group stays on the main page, below the two rows.

The rows and the 360°/video/animated parts are our own files
(cc-plinius-appearance.c, cc-plinius-panorama.c, cc-plinius-ambient.c);
their strings are in our gettext domain, so the section titles are set
in the code.

The Style page also has the background color, below the accent color
and in its look (nine colors and a color wheel for one's own, through
the color editor page of the custom accent color): primary-color with
color-shading-type 'solid', of the background and the lock screen. It
is what shows when no background is chosen: a tap on the background
shown - an own or default picture here, a video or 360° photo in our
sections - takes it away (picture-options 'none', which Phosh fills
with primary-color), no tile has a check mark then and the row on the
main page says "Color" with the color in front. Tapping the picture
again shows it again (set_background sets its placement as before).
Choosing a picture no longer writes the colors of the wallpaper (the
background color stays), so a tile counts as the current one by its
picture and placement only, and none while picture-options is 'none'
or a video or 360° photo covers it. The background color is our own
file as well (cc-plinius-bgcolor.c).
